      "quote": "optional encryption context constraint subsets"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Module-style scenario: defaults instantiate only aws_kms_key; the external/replica/replica-external keys, aliases and grants are checked as declared capabilities, including their stated configuration attributes (key material, primary key ARN, alias name/name_prefix, grantee/operations/retiring principal, encryption-context subset) via __declared__.properties. Key-policy role inputs (owners, administrators, users, service users, autoscaling roles, HMAC/asymmetric users, Route 53 DNSSEC, custom statements/override documents) are rendered by an aws_iam_policy_document data source whose statements are empty under defaults; neither data sources nor dynamic statement blocks appear in the normalised view, so these are not checked (interpreter limitation). Mutual exclusivity of the creation flags is likewise not expressible. | 2026-10-03 review: root key-policy statement also read from declared key/policy-document text (planned policy unknown in 4/6)."
